  "notes": "Top-49 processes by RSS, captured via /proc/<pid>/status VmRSS on a development image (RDK release rdk8-1.0.0, Yocto Kirkstone, kernel 6.6.104-yocto-standard+aarch64). totalRssMB (785.6) is the GROSS sum of listed processes and double-counts shared pages across processes \u2014 it does NOT equal the system-level 'used' memory (573-631 MiB across two separate snapshots per /proc/meminfo, which is the correct capacity metric per Section 3.5 MEM-006 MemAvailable guidance). onewifi_em_ctrl is the single largest RDK-B-related process, exceeding OneWifi's own base process. Several listed processes (netdata, mariadbd, ollama, apps.plugin) are development-only tooling not normative for either in-scope profile and should be excluded when sizing a production image; excluding these plus not-applicable cellular processes (ModemManager, cellularmanager) yields a plausible profile-relevant estimate of roughly 287-330 MiB. A later top(1) snapshot observed onewifi_em_ctrl at 236.9 MiB and onewifi_em_agent at 64.2 MiB (both roughly double this capture's values) \u2014 this may reflect legitimate mesh topology/client-state growth or an early leak signal; not yet distinguished, and the 72-hour soak test (MEM-008 criterion) needed to tell them apart has not been run."
